WEBVTT

00:00:00.112 --> 00:00:05.162
Here is AI Radar in action, using previously generated reports.

00:00:06.100 --> 00:00:07.862
Start with a saved frontier overview.

00:00:08.275 --> 00:00:12.062
The top-level deep-reading button opens a compact paper list.

00:00:12.450 --> 00:00:15.500
Select one paper, or add another for joint reading.

00:00:15.900 --> 00:00:20.888
Opening the collection brings those papers and their PDFs into the reading
workspace.

00:00:26.183 --> 00:00:28.171
The collection stays editable.

00:00:28.571 --> 00:00:33.471
Removing one paper changes the workspace from joint reading to single-paper
reading.

00:00:33.883 --> 00:00:37.346
New generation starts only when you press Generate report.

00:00:38.225 --> 00:00:43.538
Now we switch to a separate saved two-paper report, not a newly generated
result.

00:00:45.225 --> 00:00:50.925
This report compares two papers, keeping their identities and page counts
visible.

00:00:51.362 --> 00:00:56.312
Follow a citation, and its original excerpt now opens immediately.

00:00:56.725 --> 00:01:01.488
The paper title and physical PDF page stay attached to the evidence.

00:01:01.875 --> 00:01:05.738
The source PDF remains available for checking important claims.

00:01:10.308 --> 00:01:13.083
Discover, choose, and check the evidence.

00:01:13.496 --> 00:01:16.071
